/-!
# Leaf 3: the slit sides of a later line, in the dense form

Packet PROVE-T15-ORDDET2 (Theorem 1.5's leaf 3, `RLC.RetOrdDetStatement`; supplement p. 497, Lemma G7's proof: "the
boundary of the relative hull in `ℍ` lies on the relative trace").

At a later line of the second continuation (retained data `d` at the cutoffs `(u, r)`, `d'` at `(u, r + t)`, a chart
path `γ` of the continuation in the stop-line chart, generated by a continuous driver `W`, injective, `0 < Q <` its
lifetime, with `ψ₀ ∘ γ([0, Q]) = η₂([r, r + t])` and `ψ₀(γ(Q)) = η₂(r + t)`), the later chart inverse is
`ψ₁ = ψ₀ ∘ F̄_Q` on `ℍ̄` (`F̄_Q` the boundary extension of the Loewner inverse map `f_Q⁻¹`).

**`OrdDet.OrdSlitSideStatement` is false as stated** (it asks for a finite exceptional set): when the continuation
touches the real line between the two bases at infinitely many times (a zigzag `X₀ → X₁ → X₂ → …` of bumps moving
right, with no contact with the retained union), each touching point `Xₙ` is the vertex of a cusp of the active domain
lying on the continuation's left side, so it has a prime end `yₙ` in the left slit image with `ψ₁(yₙ) = Xₙ ∈ ℝ`.
What is true, and all the word argument needs (the word is piecewise constant with finitely many jumps), is density:

* **`exists_slitSide_of_lt`**: every open interval `(a, b)` inside the two slit images `(V̂^{0,L}_Q, 0)`,
  `(0, V̂^{0,R}_Q)` contains a point `y` with `ψ₁(y)` an interior point of the second prefix, off the first prefix and
  off the later tip (the middle chart points land on the chart path, `Lemma71P.mem_image_of_mid`; a Loewner trace has
  non-real points in every time interval, so some of them land in `ℍ`, `Lemma71P.exists_mem_H_of_lt`; the tip is a
  single prime end, `Lemma71P.eq_zero_of_extendFrom_eq_tip`). No ordinariness and no contact hypothesis is used.
* **`slitHeights_of_dense`**: with the outer word `IsRetainedWord` at the later pair, the later word has the canonical
  new-side heights `∓λ − θ₂χ` on the two slit images off its jumps.
* **`ae_retLine_facts_of_retainedWord_dense`**: the later-line facts (III-a), (III-b) of
  `OrdDet.ae_retLine_facts_of_retainedWord` with no named input.

For Theorem 1.5; uses Lemma 7.5 only (R43/R48).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

